# Baked per-office pages stay committed (repo history + tests/seo-pages.test.js)
# but must NOT deploy as static files: vercel.json rewrites run AFTER the
# filesystem check (verified against @vercel/routing-utils), so a deployed
# static /o/<CODE>/index.html would shadow the /o/:code rewrite and
# api/office-page.js would never run. The function regenerates the identical
# baked page in-memory (renderOfficePage + docs/index.html via includeFiles)
# as its fail-safe fallback, so /o/<CODE>/ never serves less than today.
docs/o

# The homepage shell. Same reason as docs/o above: vercel.json rewrites are
# evaluated AFTER the filesystem check, so a deployed static docs/index.html
# would shadow the `/` rewrite and api/home.js would never run — the homepage
# would keep serving an empty #sections shell to every crawler and agent.
#
# NOTE (verified on a preview deploy, 2026-08-21): an ignored file is also
# absent from the FUNCTION bundle — `includeFiles: "docs/index.html"` silently
# ships nothing, and both SSR handlers lose their fail-safe template. That is
# why the functions load api/_home-shell.html instead: a committed,
# byte-identical twin generated by scripts/build-offices.mjs and pinned by
# tests/seo-pages.test.js. docs/index.html stays committed as the file humans
# edit, the local-dev homepage, and the generator's input.
docs/index.html
